{"id":1157132,"docketId":490785,"caseName":"Doughty v. Maxwell","caseNameFull":"","slug":"doughty-v-maxwell","docketNumber":"422, Misc","dateFiled":"1964-02-24","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1964,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":154,"judges":"Per Curiam","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":1157132,"type":"majority","typeCode":"010combined","perCuriam":true,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1139,"isHtml":true,"text":"<div>\n<center><b><span class=\"citation multiple-matches\"><a href=\"/c/U.S./376/202/\">376 U.S. 202</a></span> (1964)</b></center>\n<center><h1>DOUGHTY<br>\nv.<br>\nMAXWELL, WARDEN.</h1></center>\n<center>No. 422, Misc.</center>\n<center><p><b>Supreme Court of United States.</b></p></center>\n<center>Decided February 24, 1964.</center>\nON PETITION FOR WRIT OF CERTIORARI TO THE SUPREME COURT OF OHIO.\n<p>Petitioner <i>pro se.</i></p>\n<p><i>William B. Saxbe,</i> Attorney General of Ohio, and <i>William C. Baird,</i> Assistant Attorney General, for respondent.</p>\n<p>PER CURIAM.</p>\n<p>The motion for leave to proceed <i>in forma pauperis</i> and the petition for writ of certiorari are granted. The judgment is reversed. <i>Carnley</i> v. <i>Cochran,</i> <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9422395\"><a href=\"/opinion/106388/carnley-v-cochran/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Carnley v. Cochran\">369 U. S. 506</a></span>, <i>Gideon</i> v. <i>Wainwright,</i> <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8945501\"><a href=\"/opinion/8954562/gideon-v-wainwright/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gideon v. Wainwright\">372 U. S. 335</a></span>.</p>\n</div>"}],"citations":[]}